cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RoT DtD Commander - Claude Code commands that carry their own DTD, an NPX installer, and the Adiutor Stop-hook doctor"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Saimonokuma"
    website: "https://github.com/Nova-Violet-Role"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Nova-Violet-Role/RoT-DtD-Commander"
license:
  - AGPL-3.0-or-later
  - EUPL-1.2
version: 3.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-02
abstract: >-
  Sixty-eight Claude Code slash commands (the nine RoT MoE lenses and their ELEVATE among them), nineteen skills and four agents whose
  answer grammar, verdict vocabulary, laws and trust boundary are declared in a
  validating XML DTD inside each file, with the shared subsets inlined at build
  time by a two-pass parameter-entity resolver. A checker holds every file to
  its own DOCTYPE in both directions (rules C1 to C14), a contract audit proves
  every declaration of the five shared subsets is used, and a guided NPX
  installer writes the set into ~/.claude with a manifest and a verified
  byte-level re-read. The Adiutor is a Stop hook plus a ledger plus a doctor
  command: it reads the DOCTYPE of the command that produced an answer, checks
  the rendered answer against it, records every run under a numbered
  append-only record, and prescribes. Eight controls trip every guard on
  purpose before the guard is trusted.
keywords:
  - "claude-code"
  - "dtd"
  - "xml"
  - "hooks"
  - "stop-hook"
  - "prompt-engineering"
  - "installer"
  - "trust-boundary"
